<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>HTML</title>
<style>
    body {
        background-color: #a9c9dd;
        font-family: "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 40px 60px;
    }

    h1 {
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 40px;
        letter-spacing: 4px;
        margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .subtitle {
        text-align: center;
        font-style: italic;
        font-weight: bold;
        color: #ffffff;
        margin-top: 5px;
        margin-bottom: 30px;
    }

    h2 {
        font-size: 26px;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    h3 {
        text-decoration: underline;
        margin-bottom: 5px;
    }

    ul {
        margin-top: 5px;
    }

    .banner-img {
        display: block;
        margin: 20px auto;
        width: 300px;
        border-radius: 4px;
    }

    .know-more {
        text-align: center;
        font-weight: bold;
        margin-top: 30px;
    }

    button {
        font-family: inherit;
        padding: 4px 10px;
        margin-left: 8px;
        cursor: pointer;
    }
</style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>HTML</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">ABOUT HyperText Markup Language</p>

    <h2>Hypertext Markup Language</h2>

    <h3>What is html?</h3>
    <p>HTML stands for Hypertext Markup Language, and is a text-based language used to structure and display web pages</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Head</li>
        <li>Body</li>
        <li>Title</li>
    </ul>

    <img class="banner-img" src="images/banner.png" alt="HTML CSS banner">

    <p>
        HTML stands for <i>Hyper Text Markup Language</i>. HTML is the standard markup language for creating Web pages.<br>
        HTML describes the structure of a Web page. HTML consists of a series of elements.<br>
        HTML elements tell the browser how to display the content.
    </p>

    <p class="know-more">
        Know more about HTML <button onclick="window.open('https://www.w3schools.com/html/','_blank')">click Here</button>
    </p>

</body>
</html>